---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
	title="About the Data — RepoTrend"
	description="How RepoTrend captures, ranks, and interprets its GitHub Trending archive."
>
	<article class="about-page">
		<header class="about-header">
			<p>Methodology and limitations</p>
			<h1>About the data</h1>
			<span>How snapshots are captured, what the metrics mean, and where gaps can occur.</span>
		</header>

		<section aria-labelledby="source-heading">
			<h2 id="source-heading">Source and scope</h2>
			<p>
				RepoTrend is an independent archive of the unfiltered, daily <a
					href="https://github.com/trending?since=daily"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
					data-analytics-surface="about_data"
				>GitHub Trending page<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span></a>. It records the
				repositories GitHub returns to an English-language request; it is not affiliated with or
				endorsed by GitHub.
			</p>
			<p>
				GitHub does not publish the ranking formula used by Trending. RepoTrend therefore archives
				the observed result and source order—it does not claim to reproduce or explain GitHub's
				algorithm.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section aria-labelledby="schedule-heading">
			<h2 id="schedule-heading">Capture schedule and timezone</h2>
			<p>
				The scheduled capture starts once each day at <strong>06:00 UTC</strong>. Dates, freshness
				notices, and capture times use UTC. Fetch jitter and processing can make the recorded time a
				few minutes later.
			</p>
			<p>
				The homepage shows the latest successfully captured snapshot, which may be older than today.
				A failed capture can be retried during the same UTC day, but GitHub does not provide RepoTrend
				with a historical Trending endpoint, so a missed day may remain a permanent gap.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section aria-labelledby="ranking-heading">
			<h2 id="ranking-heading">Ranking and rollups</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Daily rank</strong> is the repository's position in GitHub's captured source order.</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Weekly rank</strong> first favors the number of captured days a repository appeared,
					then its summed captured daily star gains. A partial-week label states how many daily
					snapshots are included.
				</li>
				<li>
					Search ordering favors exact and close name matches before broader owner, description, and
					topic matches; it is not a Trending rank.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section aria-labelledby="metrics-heading">
			<h2 id="metrics-heading">What the metrics mean</h2>
			<dl>
				<div>
					<dt>Stars gained that day</dt>
					<dd>The daily value displayed by GitHub Trending when the page was captured.</dd>
				</div>
				<div>
					<dt>Total stars and forks</dt>
					<dd>Point-in-time repository totals shown by GitHub at capture time.</dd>
				</div>
				<div>
					<dt>Captured daily star gains</dt>
					<dd>
						A sum across dates present in this archive—not lifetime growth and not an estimate for
						missing dates.
					</dd>
				</div>
				<div>
					<dt>Recorded total-star change</dt>
					<dd>The difference between the first and latest captured point-in-time totals.</dd>
				</div>
			</dl>
		</section>

		<section aria-labelledby="completeness-heading">
			<h2 id="completeness-heading">Completeness and known limits</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>An absent date means no usable snapshot was captured; it does not mean no repositories trended.</li>
				<li>Language, descriptions, counts, and source markup can be absent or change upstream.</li>
				<li>Topics are fetched separately from GitHub on a best-effort basis and may be incomplete.</li>
				<li>Comparisons describe only the two selected captures and should not be read as continuous history.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section aria-labelledby="privacy-heading">
			<h2 id="privacy-heading">Product measurement and privacy</h2>
			<p>
				RepoTrend records a small set of aggregate interaction events—search submission, archive date
				changes, empty states, completed comparisons, and outbound GitHub clicks—to find broken or
					unused journeys. Event payloads contain the event name, interface surface, and URL path only;
					they do not include search terms, repository queries, user identifiers, or the URL query string.
			</p>
		</section>

		<nav class="about-actions" aria-label="About page actions">
			<a href="/trending">Browse the archive</a>
			<a href="/compare">Compare snapshots</a>
		</nav>
	</article>
</Layout>

<style>
	.about-page {
		max-width: 48rem;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}

	.about-header {
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.about-header p,
	.about-header h1,
	.about-header span {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.about-header p {
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0.05em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.about-header h1 {
		font-size: 2rem;
	}

	.about-header span {
		display: block;
		margin-top: 0.375rem;
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
	}

	.about-page section {
		margin-top: 1.75rem;
		padding-top: 1.5rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
	}

	.about-page h2 {
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
		font-size: 1.25rem;
	}

	.about-page p,
	.about-page ul,
	.about-page dl {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.about-page p + p {
		margin-top: 0.75rem;
	}

	.about-page p,
	.about-page li,
	.about-page dd {
		line-height: 1.65;
	}

	.about-page ul {
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
	}

	.about-page li + li {
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
	}

	.about-page a {
		color: var(--color-link);
	}

	.about-page dl {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	.about-page dl > div {
		padding: 0.875rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-radius: 6px;
		background: var(--color-bg-secondary);
	}

	.about-page dt {
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	.about-page dd {
		margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
		font-size: 0.875rem;
	}

	.about-actions {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}

	.about-actions a {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		min-height: 44px;
		padding: 0.625rem 1rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-radius: 6px;
		font-weight: 600;
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	.about-actions a:first-child {
		border-color: var(--color-accent);
		background: var(--color-accent);
		color: var(--color-accent-text);
	}

	@media (max-width: 640px) {
		.about-page dl {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
